{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 33, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "Hark a journey to the Land of the Rising Sun a most wondrous quest I shall now unfold for thee.\n\n**Day First Tokyo's Grandeur**\n\nFrom distant shores thou shalt arrive in Tokyo's heart.\nA bustling city a most vibrant start.\nThe Shinjuku Gyoen a garden serene and fair.\nThen Shibuya's crossing a spectacle rare.\nDinner awaits in Ginza's bright array.\nA taste of Japan to light thy day.\n\n**Day Second Ancient Temples**\n\nTo Asakusa we venture a temple old and wise.\nSenso-ji's grandeur doth meet thine eyes.\nUeno Park a haven calm and green.\nMuseums abound a cultured scene.\nAkihabara's electric a gamer's delight.\nThen Sumida River bathed in evening light.\n\n**Day Third Hakone's Mountain Majesty**\n\nHakone's peaks beckon a vista grand.\nMount Fuji's form a sight so planned.\nA cruise upon Lake Ashi a tranquil grace.\nVolcanic hot springs a soothing space.\nArt museums abound a visual treat.\nNature's embrace both bitter and sweet.\n\n**Day Fourth Kyoto's Imperial Charm**\n\nBy bullet train we speed to Kyoto's keep.\nWhere ancient traditions softly sleep.\nFushimi Inari's gates a vermillion dream.\nA thousand pathways a flowing stream.\nKiyomizu-dera's temple a wooden grace.\nA panoramic view of time and space.\n\n**Day Fifth Gion's Geisha Dance**\n\nIn Gion's district wander with care.\nHoping a Geisha thou might spy there.\nKiyomizu-dera's beauty doth endure.\nPhilosopher's Path a tranquil lure.\nNijo Castle's splendor a shogun's hold.\nStories of old bravely told.\n\n**Day Sixth Nara's Deer Park**\n\nTo Nara we journey where deer roam free.\nTodai-ji Temple's giant Buddha to see.\nKasuga Taisha's lanterns a shining sight.\nAncient history bathed in golden light.\nA peaceful respite a gentle pace.\nIn nature's embrace find solace and grace.\n\n**Day Seventh Osaka's Culinary Delights**\n\nOsaka's vibrant spirit doth call.\nDotonbori's lights enth